Interface methods in Java are implicitly public. The explicit "public" keyword on these method declarations is redundant and inconsistent with other interfaces in the codebase (e.g., CodeAttributesGetter, MessagingAttributesGetter, DbClientAttributesGetter). Remove the "public" modifiers from these method declarations.
```suggestion
  boolean isEmpty();

  @Nullable
  String resolveService(String host, @Nullable Integer port, Supplier<String> pathSupplier);
```

